# Obsessive-grade field model

## Mouse — geometry and fit
- length, max width, grip width at front/mid/rear, height, front button height
- hump peak position (normalized X), hump width/radius, rear flare, front flare
- side curvature, side-wall angle, comfort grooves, ergo tilt, ledges/rests
- sensor X/Y position relative to grip center
- center of gravity X/Y and lift balance
- 1-2-2 vs 1-3-1 suitability; ring/pinky clearance
- palm / relaxed claw / aggressive claw / pincer claw / knuckle claw / fingertip vectors
- hand length and width bands, plus ratio-based fit

## Mouse — implementation
- total weight and unit variance; shell material/perforation
- coating + dry/sweaty behavior + long-term wear
- sensor model, MCU, firmware, motion sync, ripple control, angle snapping, LOD/landing distance
- supported and *stable measured* polling rates; high-poll dongle included/optional
- click latency by connection, sensor start/mid/end delay, CPI error/deviation
- main switch model/type, actuation force curve, pre-travel, post-travel/total travel, wobble
- side-button switch, position, force and travel
- encoder make/height, wheel step tactility, wheel click force, free-spin/tilt if present
- debounce range, eager/deferred modes, slam-click protection
- battery capacity and runtime by polling mode; charging behavior
- stock skate material/geometry/thickness; spare feet/grips
- software/web driver, OS support, onboard profiles, remapping limits
- QC signals: flex, creak, click grinding, wheel wobble, coating variance, revision notes

## Mousepad
- surface class: cloth / hybrid / glass / resin / plastic
- weave/finish/coating/treatment and actual surface material
- static friction / initial-speed index and dynamic-friction / glide-speed index separately
- stopping power as its own derived axis, not a synonym for speed
- X/Y friction ratio and directional feel
- texture/abrasiveness, skin friction, sleeve friction and noise
- humidity/sweat sensitivity, temperature sensitivity, static-electricity behavior
- base material, durometer/Shore measurement, xsoft/soft/mid/firm label, thickness
- pressure response/sink curve and effect on braking
- edge stitch height/recess, corner radius, flatness, base grip
- break-in curve, worn-zone behavior, cleaning recovery, coating life
- sensor tracking exceptions and skate/material dependencies

## Skates
- material: pure PTFE, hardened PTFE, UHMW-PE, glass, ceramic/sapphire/other
- purity/treatment when documented; edge rounding; thickness
- dot/donut/full-size geometry, diameter, contact area and number of pieces
- cushion layer, anti-collapse layer, adhesive type
- static/dynamic speed by pad class, stopping, noise, vibration, dust sensitivity
- wear rate on cloth/hybrid/glass; break-in curve
- compatibility matrix for pad material and base softness

## User profile
- hand length + width; optional finger lengths
- grip subtype and actual palm contact points
- finger layout 1-2-2 / 1-3-1
- current mouse + liked/disliked traits (relative recommendation mode)
- wrist / hybrid / arm aim; sensitivity as cm/360; DPI/CPI
- games and input pattern (tac FPS, tracking, MOBA click-spam, productivity)
- desired weight, click force, wheel tactility, side-button priority, connectivity
- display refresh + CPU tier when evaluating >1 kHz polling value
- dry/sweaty hands, texture tolerance, sleeve use, ambient humidity
- pressure habit on pad, preferred stopping behavior, pad size/desk constraint
- budget and region/availability
